  "findings": [
    "s8..s40 carry the33 packet words without later scalar overwrites; s34/s35 only receive getPC and the paired low/carry add.",
    "All nine before and after tag captures address the intended logical VGPR/lane under validated bank history. Initialization vector writes are each followed by wait-idle.",
    "The full64-bit intended return address uses the assembled20-byte label delta, including the literal add instruction, and lands exactly on the post-slot MODE read.",
    "STATUS reads have wait-idle; MODE and EXEC are captured before clearing banks/reducing EXEC for output.",
    "All33 stores use bank0, vaddr0, one active lane and the captured output pointer; wait-idle precedes each store and storecnt0 precedes data-register reuse.",
    "The one8-byte output-pointer ABI, wave32,528 allocated VGPRs and42-SGPR metadata cover every shader register and match the host configuration."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Static instruction/ABI proof does not measure whether a trap occurs or how installed hardware executes the handler.",
    "Trap effects are deliberately observed through saved before/after state; unchanged SGPR or VGPR state across a real handler is not assumed as an empirical fact.",
    "Independent ELF section, descriptor and MessagePack parsers are pinned inherited tools; this reviewer reconciled all instruction bytes and semantic capture/store invariants."
  ]
